# Keys allowed to sign Pandora run verdicts, for .github/actions/pandora-verdict.
#
# One key per line, in ssh-keygen's allowed signers format, with the principal
# and the namespace both pandora-verdict:
#
#   pandora-verdict namespaces="pandora-verdict" ssh-ed25519 AAAA... pandora-verdict
#
# The key is the worker's verdict key: `pandora worker status` prints it under
# `verdict signer:`. The private half never leaves the worker's engine root.
#
# CI reads this file from the default branch only, never from a pull request's
# head or base, so a key takes effect only after it is merged there, and
# revoking a key means removing its line on the default branch. With no key
# line here, every verification answers verified=false reason=no_signers and
# the suite runs.
